cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the CMRM Virtual Rhythm Lab in teaching or research, please cite this software."
title: "CMRM Virtual Rhythm Lab"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sarti"
    given-names: "Augusto"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
repository-code: "https://github.com/augusto-sarti/CMRM-Virtual-Rhythm-Lab"
abstract: >-
  Interactive teaching notebooks accompanying Computer Music Representations
  and Models (CMRM), with experiments on onset evidence, periodicity,
  autocorrelation, phase autocorrelation, rhythmograms, beat tracking,
  polymetric structure, rhythmic clusters, and the Sound of Muzak case study.
  Original rhythm-analysis material and the synthetic Sound of Muzak example
  include contributions by Bruno Di Giorgi. The APM influence-set interpretation
  includes contributions by Riccardo Gianpiccolo.
keywords:
  - rhythm analysis
  - computer music
  - music information retrieval
  - autocorrelation
  - phase autocorrelation
  - beat tracking
  - polymeter
  - Jupyter
  - teaching software
